## Unreleased

- Skip the two full-size copies chroma upsampling used to make when nothing
  needs upsampling, which is every component of a 4:4:4 image. This was 38% of
  decode time; see JPEG-PERFORMANCE.md for measurements and for what
  dominates the rest.
- Fix the GIF decoder. An image descriptor's local colour table was being
  read *after* the LZW minimum code size, so any frame that carried a local
  colour table was decoded from the wrong offset; this made every frame but
  the first of most animations fail. Interlaced images are now decoded
  instead of being refused, disposal method 3 (restore to previous) is
  implemented instead of being reported as an invalid bit pattern, comment
  and plain text extensions are skipped rather than refused, and a stray
  debug print has been removed from the disposal handling.
- Add a pure OCaml JPEG codec: baseline sequential and progressive DCT
  decoding (8-bit samples, arbitrary chroma subsampling, restart intervals)
  and baseline sequential encoding.  JPEG is now handled natively by
  `ImageLib`, so the `imagemagick` fallback is no longer used for it.
- `ImageLib` now accepts the format extension with or without a leading dot
  (and in any case). Previously a bare extension such as `"png"` raised
  `Not_yet_implemented` because dispatch matched the dotted forms only; this
  is what made the newly-added JPEG path look as if it broke PNG.

